{#
	A page that shows live data refreshes itself in place, with htmx. This is what refreshes it, and what says so, with Pause.
	It asks for the address in use, so it follows every change of card, search or page, and window.cattoLive holds it back
	while the reader is reading or typing. The page's script counts the seconds (data-live-seconds) and asks, because
	htmx's own condition is code it compiles, which the content policy refuses. It is shown only with JavaScript. Its
	request carries X-Live-Refresh, and the controller marks it as no visit (Http\LiveRefresh::notAVisit).
	live_seconds: 15 for a list of what is happening now, 30 for figures and for records that a job changes once a minute.
	live_held: what it says while it holds still because the reader has opened something marked data-live-hold (such as a
	row opened to read what an address did, which a refresh would otherwise close); optional.
#}
<div id="catto-live" class="cl-live-status small" data-live-status hidden hx-morph-skip
     data-live-seconds="{{ live_seconds }}" hx-get="" hx-trigger="catto-live-refresh"
     hx-target="#cl-main" hx-select="#cl-main" hx-swap="outerMorph" hx-sync="#cl-main:drop"
     hx-headers='{"X-Live-Refresh":"1"}' hx-status:4xx="swap:none" hx-status:5xx="swap:none">
	<span class="cl-live-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
	<span data-live-running>Updates by itself every {{ live_seconds }} seconds.</span>
	{% if live_held|default('') %}<span data-live-held hidden>{{ live_held }}</span>{% endif %}
	<span data-live-paused hidden>Paused. It stays as it is until you press Resume.</span>
	<span data-live-when></span>
	{{ ui('action.button', {label: 'Pause', type: 'button', icon: 'action-pause', id: 'live-pause', variant: 'secondary', size: 'small'}) }}
	{{ ui('action.button', {label: 'Resume', type: 'button', icon: 'action-play', id: 'live-resume', variant: 'secondary', size: 'small', hidden: true}) }}
</div>
